# Pinned architecture decisions. A later agent reads this first and conforms.

project: ProxID
languages: [python, typescript]
strict_uniform_casing: false

## Backend (python, .py, snake_case)

layers:
  routers:  backend/app/api/v1/endpoints
  schemas:  backend/app/schemas
  services: backend/app/services
  crud:     backend/app/crud
  entities: backend/app/models
  core:     backend/app/core
  middleware: backend/app/middleware

composition_root: backend/app/core/container.py
entry_point: backend/app/main.py
migrations: backend/alembic/versions
architecture_check: python backend/arch_check.py
test_command: cd backend && python -m pytest -q

### Rules the checker enforces

1. endpoints may import schemas, services, core. Never crud, never models.
2. services may import crud, schemas, models, core, other services only through
   the use-case service, never a second entity's service. A service never
   imports a database driver (asyncpg, psycopg2) and never builds an engine.
3. crud may import models, schemas, core. Never services, never endpoints,
   never another entity's crud module.
4. models import sqlalchemy and core only. Never schemas, crud, services.
5. schemas import pydantic and core only. Never models, crud, services.
6. Raw SQL strings live only in crud.
7. Feature flags are read only in core/config.py. No os.getenv elsewhere.
8. No emoji and no non-ASCII in source, comments, or user-facing strings.

## Frontend (typescript, .ts/.tsx, camelCase)

layers:
  entities:     frontend/src/types
  schemas:      frontend/src/lib/contracts
  crud:         frontend/src/services      (transport to the backend)
  services:     frontend/src/hooks         (business logic, query composition)
  routers:      frontend/src/pages         (route entry points)
  presentation: frontend/src/components

Rules:
1. pages and components never import src/services or src/lib/api directly.
   They use hooks.
2. hooks never call fetch/axios. They call src/services.
3. services never import React, hooks, components, or pages.
4. types import nothing.
5. architecture_check: node frontend/scripts/arch-check.mjs

## Coexisting framework directories

backend/alembic is Alembic's own directory and lives alongside the layout.
frontend/src/components/ui is the primitive set (button, card, input); it is
presentation only and is imported by pages and components, never the reverse.

## Deliberate deviations from house-standard.md

- The architecture check is a dependency-free AST/source scanner rather than
  import-linter. It enforces every layer contract import-linter would, plus the
  emoji, banned-name, raw-SQL-placement and config-flag-placement rules that
  import-linter cannot express. One command, no extra install.
